      "title": "Assuming Bias and Responsible AI",
      "summary": "There are plenty of examples of artificial intelligence and machine learning systems that made it into the news because of biased predictions and failures. Here are a few examples on AI/ML gone wrong: Amazon had an AI recruiting tool which favored men over women for technical jobs The Microsoft chat bot named “Tay” which turned racist and sexist rather quickly A doctor at the Jupiter Hospital in Florida referred to IBM’s AI system for helping recommend cancer treatments as “a piece of sh*t” Facebook’s AI got someone arrested for incorrectly translating text The list of AI failures goes on…",
