      "title": "Abusing Application Layer Gateways (NAT Slipstreaming)",
      "summary": "You might have heard about “NAT Slipstreaming” by Samy Kamkar. It’s an amazing technique that allows punching a hole in your routers firewall by just visiting a website. The attack depends on the router having the Application Layer Gateway enabled. This gateway can be used by anyone inside your network to open a firewall port (totally by design). Protocols such as SIP ( Session Initiation Protocol ) use it. What I will focus on in this post is the Application Layer Gateway ( ALG ) and SIP . In particular to understand how these can be abused by an adversary.",
